<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-recorder-reported-outcomes> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementSeverity> <urn:usf:requirement-severity:blocking> <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-recorder> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-recorder-reported-outcomes> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:validation> <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-recorder> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-recorder-reported-outcomes> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "The factory always emits acceptedOutcome null, evidenceIdentity null, contributionDigest null, tokenFact/cacheFact/costFact null, parentAttemptIdentity null and overlapDisposition unknown. Start and finish have outcomeLineage null; failure and interrupted carry only their corresponding reported lifecycle lineage failed/interrupted, not observed semantic nonacceptance. For a start require null end/duration/finishedAt. For a terminal compute safe duration only when both nonnegative offsets are known and end>=start; otherwise retain null duration. intervals.total is that reported duration and all phase subintervals remain null. Use fixed bounded missingness text identifying unknown duration/acceptance/resource facts; never caller prose." <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-recorder> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-recorder-reported-outcomes> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-recorder> .
